From d02657c8376916b0294573faf9b486904fd599f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:45:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: Keep ConPTY input connected during descendant lifecycle
 checks

The lifecycle fixture tests termination and normal-exit preservation. Keep its terminal input connected while PowerShell starts, rather than introducing early EOF into both scenarios. Commands, permissions, readiness deadlines and descendant assertions remain unchanged.

Native control 40055759331 executes all three lifecycle tests and both TTY phases on Windows2022 and Windows Latest. Earlier unchanged-input controls fail latest before parent-entered. This is fixture correction; closed-input production behavior is not claimed repaired.
---
 codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/unified_exec/tests.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/unified_exec/tests.rs b/codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/unified_exec/tests.rs
index be2d1bf0..8de05873 100644
--- a/codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/unified_exec/tests.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/src/unified_exec/tests.rs
@@ -980,7 +980,7 @@ async fn assert_legacy_tty_descendant_lifecycle(
         &[],
         &[],
         /*tty*/ true,
-        /*stdin_open*/ false,
+        /*stdin_open*/ true,
     )
     .await
     .expect("spawn legacy sandbox ConPTY lifecycle test");
